Subject: [PATCH 0960/3799] soh: rename D_80A24E48 -> sDistMultipliersExtra
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: a single unreferenced 1.8f directly after sDistMultipliers, which ends at 1.7f — it continues that table's 0.1 progression, so it looks like its cut-off thirteenth entry.
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ganon_Mant/z_en_ganon_mant.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ganon_Mant/z_en_ganon_mant.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ganon_Mant/z_en_ganon_mant.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ganon_Mant/z_en_ganon_mant.c
index 01b2b075e..e0d5040e9 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ganon_Mant/z_en_ganon_mant.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Ganon_Mant/z_en_ganon_mant.c
@@ -81,7 +81,8 @@ static f32 sDistMultipliers[GANON_MANT_NUM_JOINTS] = {
     0.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.1f, 1.2f, 1.3f, 1.4f, 1.5f, 1.6f, 1.7f,
 };
 
-static f32 D_80A24E48[] = {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was D_80A24E48: a single unreferenced 1.8f directly after sDistMultipliers, which ends at 1.7f — it continues that table's 0.1 progression, so it looks like its cut-off thirteenth entry.
+static f32 sDistMultipliersExtra[] = {  // was D_80A24E48 [LLM:GUESS]
     1.8f,
 };
 
